      "title": "Troubleshooting TLS Connectivity and Handshake Failures in Admin Console",
      "content_summary": "Guidance for resolving connection resets, TLS handshake errors, and certificate warnings when accessing the Admin Console, focusing on DNS, network, and certificate issues.",
      "content_body": "When users report connection refused or reset errors alongside HTTP 502 responses, first verify that the client can resolve the Admin Console hostname correctly, as incorrect DNS configuration is a common root cause. Check for expired certificate warnings during the TLS handshake, which typically requires a certificate renewal from the internal CA or cloud provider. If DNS and certificates are valid, investigate network configuration errors such as missing firewall rules or load balancer misconfigurations that block secure traffic. Adjusting the load balancer's SSL termination settings or correcting firewall allow-lists usually resolves the underlying connectivity issue."
